# Frontend

- React + Vite + TypeScript strict
- UI primitives from `@agency/ui`; shared types from `@agency/shared`
- No business logic duplication — call the API; do not reimplement domain rules in components
- Never import Nest internals, Prisma, or vendor SDKs (Stripe, OpenAI, WHM, etc.)
- Never put backend secrets or API keys in frontend code or Vite env that is exposed to the client
- Keep route/page files thin; extract hooks and presentational pieces
- Respect surface boundaries: no admin capabilities in portal; no portal billing UI on the public site (login entry is OK)
- Auth UX may use HTTP-only cookies; do not store long-lived tokens in `localStorage` by default
